1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,200
Today, AI agents write code at superhuman speed,

2
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:08,800
and CI systems dutifully flash green.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,200
But green tests alone cannot prove an AI patch

4
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:16,500
actually fixed the intended problem.

5
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,200
What if the test was already passing?

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,800
What if assertions were weakened?

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
If the patch matters, the base must break.

8
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:29,200
Meet Basebreak: a causal verification runtime for AI-written code.

9
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,800
Instead of trusting green CI, Basebreak evaluates the change

10
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:37,200
across three isolated execution worlds:

11
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,000
First, the Base world must fail under a sealed witness,

12
00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:43,200
reproducing the defect.

13
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,200
Second, the Candidate world must pass.

14
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,800
Third, reverting the patch delta in a counterfactual world must fail again,

15
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:53,000
proving the patch was strictly necessary.

16
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:57,200
Here is Basebreak verifying ResetVault, our synthetic security-sensitive scenario.

17
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:02,000
The AI model—NVIDIA's Nemotron 3.5 Lightning hosted on Nebius Token Factory—

18
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,800
generates the candidate fix.

19
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,200
Basebreak parses the proposal via pure static AST inspection,

20
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:13,800
then orchestrates eleven isolated operations across Nebius microVM sandboxes.

21
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,200
Base fails with exit 1.

22
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:20,500
The candidate passes exit 0 in forty milliseconds.

23
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:23,800
And the counterfactual fails with exit 1.

24
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:28,200
Anyone can verify this outcome without logging in.

25
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:32,800
Hosted globally on Cloudflare Workers, Basebreak's public Judge dashboard

26
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:35,500
presents the complete causal receipt.

27
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:39,500
Every run binds the exact source commit, candidate tree digest,

28
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:43,500
and sandbox outputs into a cryptographic verification receipt, authenticated with a

29
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,500
verifier-signed custom RSA-2048 proof and committed to an SQLite Durable Object ledger.

30
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:51,500
Transparent, auditable, and independently reproducible.

31
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,500
For advisory grounding on security fixes like CVE-2024-21626,

32
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:59,500
Basebreak integrates Tavily Search.

33
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:04,500
Tavily grounds and binds authoritative advisory information from NIST and GitHub

34
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:07,800
to an already frozen contract.

35
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,200
Our deterministic firewall guarantees external web claims never override code execution.

36
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:16,500
Web grounding provides advisory context; independent sandbox execution governs the verdict.

37
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,500
Basebreak transforms AI code generation from probabilistic guessing

38
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:25,000
into empirical causal verification under sealed witnesses.

39
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:30,200
Powered by NVIDIA Nemotron, Nebius Token Factory Sandboxes, and Cloudflare Workers,

40
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:34,500
it is the verification layer modern coding agents have been missing.

41
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:39,500
Remember: If the patch matters, the base must break.
